   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Live Code Compilation\n\nSplit screen: code is typed on the left and the button on the right snaps to match on the exact frame each property finishes. On a tall frame the split stacks (code on top, preview below).\n\nCategory: compositions. Length: 8.667 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- You want cause and effect for a developer audience: a style prop finishes typing on the left and the button on the right changes on that exact frame.\n- The pitch needs an HMR moment where every property lands as a hard snap rather than an ease.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The code on screen has to be yours: the typed fragments and the resulting button are fixed here; use glass-code-block or glass-code-walk with your own code.\n- The shot is about commands and their output: use a terminal block.\n\nVariables:\n- accent_color (color): Accent, default \"#3b82f6\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
